# The catalog's artifact trees: `stark sync` writes them from a stark-skills checkout,
# and the next sync overwrites a hand-edit (no bifrost gate catches one — CI runs
# validate / build --check / check-bumps; `sync --check` runs only in stark-skills'
# marketplace-sync, immediately after it regenerates). Marking them collapses them in a
# sync PR's diff, and stark-skills' `findings_review_post.ts` reads these rows at the PR
# head and reports findings on these paths in the review BODY rather than an inline
# thread that `required_conversation_resolution` turns into a publish blocker.
# Deliberately NOT here: catalog/*/bundle.yaml, catalog/*/mcp/** and catalog/*/agents/**
# — all curated (`runSync` manages only skills/ and commands/). See CLAUDE.md's Layout
# entry for what these rows do NOT do: they neither weaken a CODEOWNERS gate nor, on
# their own, decide routing (stark-skills adds `catalog/**` for this repo).
catalog/*/skills/** linguist-generated=true
catalog/*/commands/** linguist-generated=true
vendor/** linguist-generated=true
index.json linguist-generated=true
bundles/** linguist-generated=true
.claude-plugin/** linguist-generated=true
